/*
:name: selfref_wire
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: selfref_wire
:pyrope_top: selfref_wire
*/

// 2c-wire / Type-C self-reference, the packed-VECTOR form. The golden's
//     wire [3:0] t;  assign t = {t[2], t[1], t[0], a[0]};
// is a word-level "loop" that is ACYCLIC bit by bit, so t settles at {4{a[0]}}
// (confirmed against iverilog). This Pyrope states that settled value directly.
//
// The packed-ARRAY form of the same false cycle was fixed in 2026-06 (see
// array_selfref.v); the VECTOR form was not, and it fell through BOTH gates of
// the continuous-assign cycle classifier -- it has only ONE writer and a
// whole-net (NamedValue) LHS. Left as a `mut`, every sibling-bit read bound to
// the net's `0sb?` poison init and only the one lane with a non-self operand
// survived: lhd emitted `y = {1'b?,1'b?,1'b?,a[0]}` with exit 0 and no
// diagnostic -- a silent MISCOMPILE of legal Verilog.
//
// It is not a toy shape: firtool emits it for every bit-sliced AES/SM4 S-box in
// xiangshan, and it is why `lhd lec --set formal.solver=lgyosys` REFUTED
// BlockCipherModule/CryptoModule while cvc5 PROVED them. cvc5 may choose the
// implementation's X, so it cannot see a lowering that only lost DEFINEDNESS --
// which is exactly why a second engine's refutation is treated as authoritative.
//
// prp-v2prp2v-selfref_wire is the load-bearing half: it reads the golden BACK
// through the Verilog front end, which is where the defect lived.

pub comb selfref_wire(a:u4) -> (y:u4) {
  mut b:u1 = a#[0..=0]
  y = (b << 3) | (b << 2) | (b << 1) | b
}
